 ### Variable Gaussian Blurring
-A reconstruction technique used to reduce visible artifacts from the discrete sampled nature of volume models, specifically false low frequencies caused by the Nyquist limit [S6, unofficial]. It applies variable Gaussian blurring to the source volume models before or during reconstruction to high-resolution 2D images [S6, unofficial]. The Nyquist limit is defined as half the sampling rate; infinite sampling of continuous surfaces is the only way to completely avoid artifacts, but blurring mitigates the visible effects of discrete sampling [S6, unofficial].
