 ### Interpolation Schemes for Projection-Slice Resampling
-Resampling filters applied to extracted projection-slices to control ghosting artifacts and rendering quality during Fourier volume rendering [S8].
-*   **Point-sampling (Nearest-neighbor):** Clamps missing samples to the nearest available value, causing apparent ghosting artifacts when the volume is rotated [S8].
-*   **Trilinear Interpolation:** Reduces replica intensities and ghosting artifacts compared to point-sampling, with similar performance for slice sizes $\le 512^2$ but higher cost for larger volumes [S8].
-*   **Hamming Windowed-Sinc (Width 5):** A high-order reconstruction filter that maximally reduces ghosting artifacts when combined with zero-padding [S8].
-Point-sampling and trilinear interpolation have nearly identical performance for slice sizes $\le 512^2$, but trilinear incurs higher performance overhead for larger volumes [S8].
